# Project Sentinel — Always-On Policy

**Updated:** 2026-08-06 (Prompt 7 rule budget). Sole `alwaysApply: true` rule — hard cap 120 lines.

Official Ultra docs + **live platform fields** outrank this file. Detail lives in
`.cursor/rules/Sentinel_Ultra_Policy_Detail.mdc`, role workflows, and
`.cursor/skills/sentinel-ultra-review/reference/`. If those conflict with this file on the
items below, follow this file.

## Submitter verdicts (do not mix with reviewer outcomes)

- **Valid as-is** — instruction, tests, oracle, environment, and source PR align; no rewrite; local oracle `1.0` / NOP `0.0` when required.
- **Fixable** — all defects correctable in allowed task files without reducing/replacing PR scope.
- **Not Fixable** — validity requires scope reduction/replacement, or a disallowed/unrecoverable environment problem.

## Four core principles

- **Solvability** — solvable from the instruction and pinned repo without arbitrary guessing.
- **Clarity & No Leakage** — behavior and contracts, not implementation spoilers or verifier internals.
- **Verifiability** — every requirement tested; every assertion stated or reasonably implied; deterministic; no gaming.
- **Authenticity** — real engineering work grounded in the source PR (expand scope only; never replace).

## Agent Judge bar

- Blocking axes: **`test_coverage`** and **`test_faithfulness`**.
- Internal revision bar: drive **every** Agent Judge axis to **≥ 3.5** before treating Difficulty as in-scope (P-010 / P-011). Judge runs before Difficulty.

## Task metadata limits

| Field | Limit |
|-------|--------|
| `cpus` | 2 or 4 |
| `memory_mb` | 2048–16384 |
| `storage_mb` | 5120–10240 |
| `gpus` | always 0 |
| `build_timeout_sec` | ≤ 1800 |
| `agent.timeout_sec` | ≤ **7200** |
| `verifier.timeout_sec` | ≤ 1800 |
| Harbor network | `[environment]=public`; `[agent]=allowlist` + `allowed_hosts=["api.portkey.ai"]`; `[verifier]=no-network` |
| Compose | remove `network_mode="none"` from `docker_compose.yaml` if present |

Check **all** metadata fields — not only source/timeouts. Full narrative: `reference/harbor-format.md`.

## Never

- Never edit tracked source files in `environment/repo/`.
- Never reduce or replace PR scope (expand only when allowed).
- Never invent oracle/NOP rewards or timings.
- Never mix submitter and reviewer verdict systems (or legacy Valid/Invalid labels on Ultra forms).

